## Review rework

- Serialized socket progress behind one queued owner. Forced overlapping service calls now prove exact-once partial writes and maximum socket-write concurrency of one.
- Tracked channel pointer users across suspension. One read per channel stream is enforced; queued writes reserve against the per-channel cap; cancel/reset/close marks a typed disposition, waits for pending users, and then frees. Connect, channel-open, session-operation, and teardown drain paths are likewise serialized.
- Applied the overall upload deadline and source chunk bound. Replaced the structured timeout race that waited for a non-cooperative cancelled child with a prompt cancellation/timeout race. External signer tasks are explicitly tracked, notification-driven, cancelled, and joined during teardown.
- Applied `allowedConsecutiveMisses` to automatic keepalive failures before connection-fatal teardown. Preserved the active connect phase before teardown and populated timeout/cancellation counters plus pending-open/read/write and queued-byte gauges.
- Added regressions for concurrent bridge service, signer join, resolution timeout phase/counter cleanup, and twenty repeated connect-cancel cycles. The focused adapter suite now has 11 passing tests.

