Static review found a remaining teardown race: the timeout helper returns before a non-cooperative socket service task finishes, while teardown clears the same bridge buffers. A late write completion can then remove bytes from an emptied buffer, and the pending service task is not joined. I’m still running every claimed gate so the verdict includes real exit codes rather than substituting static reasoning for validation.
